1 NOTE My 26 great grand father.
2 CONT
2 CONT Great friend and advisor of Pope Victor III. Considered to have started the Crusades.
2 CONT
2 CONT "The fact that it is Pope Victor III who in fact initiated what later became the Crusades on the advice of Elchanan, his Jewish councillor, is extremely relevant to historical documents and facts concerning the connection between 
2 CONC Rashi (Elchanan's first cousin) and early Crusaders."
2 CONT
2 CONT See Shlomo Yitzhaki TZARFATI, Meir KALONYMOS, Godfrey V "The Crusader" OF BOULOGNE and Baldwin I OF BOULOGNE.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Gentiles called him Felix, because he was "always happy". His nickname "the Jewish Pope" gave birth to numerous (obviously false) legends about him replacing Victor III as the Pope after his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ancestor of the Spira family. The name Spira derives from Speyer, a city in Germany. To check his descendents, go to Shmuel SPIRA.
