2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT The Ribam (c. 1090 – c. 1130), Rabbi Yitzchak ben Meir, was one of the Baalei Tosafos. He was the grandson of Rashi, and brother of the Rashbam and the Rabbeinu Tam. His father was Meir ben Shmuel and his mother was Yocheved, the 
2 CONC daughter of Rashi. He died before his father, leaving four children (Jacob Tam, Sefer ha-Yashar, No. 616, p. 72b, Vienna, 1811). Although he died young, the Ribam contributed to Tosafos, mentioned by Eliezer b. Joel ha-Levi (Abi h
2 CONC a-'Ezri, §417), to several tractates of the Talmud. Isaac himself is often quoted in the edited Tosafos (Shab. 138a; Ket. 29b et passim).
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT The widow of RIBAM (who died young) married Rabbi Yehuda of Paris (c.1130 - 1124)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
