2 CONT
2 CONT Rav Abba Family Tree
2 CONT
2 CONT Thanks to David H. KELLEY and Alisa SHARON alisa_Sharon at yahoo.com for information on this page.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jehuda from Lombardy (b. 635) had a son Kolonimus (b. 685).
2 CONT
2 CONT Kolonimus from Italy had a son Mushulam (b. 720).
2 CONT
2 CONT Mushulam the great from Luka, Italy had a son also called Kolonimus (b. 765).
2 CONT
2 CONT This Kolonimus, Gaon from Luka, Italy had a son Moshe HAZAKEN (b. 810).
2 CONT
2 CONT Moshe the Elder of Luka had a son called Kononimus of Luka (b. 855).
2 CONT
2 CONT This Kolonimus of Luka had a son Meshulam (b. 900).
2 CONT
2 CONT R. Mushulam the great had a son Abun (b. 935).
2 CONT
2 CONT Rabana Abun (Abba), the Great Prince of Le Mans, Prince of the House of David had children:
2 CONT
2 CONT R. Joshua
2 CONT   R. Isaac
2 CONT     R. Eleazar the Great
2 CONT       Isaac
2 CONT           Kalonymos, from Mainz to Speyer (b. 1096, d. 1127)
2 CONT
2 CONT R. Isaac the great, b. 955 (at the time of Seadya Gaon)
2 CONT    Shimon b. 975 a great poet
2 CONT          Joseph (b. 995 France)
2 CONT                R. Simeon the Great of Mainz. (According to David H. Kelley, R. Simeon was the son of R. Isaac.)
2 CONT                daughter (b. 1015) married Isaac, parents of RASHI
2 CONT          Elchanan, according to the legend was kidnapped to Christianity and was a pope.
2 CONT
2 CONT R. Abun described above, may be one and the same person as R. Abun, Head of the Yeshiva of Narbonne, whose son was:
2 CONT
2 CONT R. Moses (Narbonne)
2 CONT * R. Jacob, Prophet, Gaon
2 CONT           * R. Moses, ha Darshan.
2 CONT                * R. Judah, ha-Darshan.
2 CONT                     *    R. LEVI
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.loebtree.com/abba.html
