1 NOTE My 26 great grandfather.
2 CONT
2 CONT The name Frances seems to be variation of the names "of Francia", "of the Franks"... since it has been used sporadically as an equivalent of these names among the Frankish royal family since the III th century... (see Walter OF TH
2 CONC E EAST FRANKS, for example). These Frankish origins are emphasized by the royal lily on the Frances coat of arms.
2 CONT
2 CONT " The origins go back to 1137 at least, with an account of an act of homage paid by the town’s inhabitants to the Count of Barcelona in which is mentioned a Jewish lord from north of the Pyrenees whose surname was Frances (Frenchm
2 CONC an, Frank man). "
