1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Vivant (a literal translation into medieval French of "Hayyim") of Meaux is mentioned in the tax roll of Paris in 1292, as mentioned below.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is the same person as Rabbi Yehiel of Paris (Many genealogical details found on https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yechiel_of_Paris), who was known as Vivant Meldensis (Latin for somebody coming from Meaux).
2 CONT
2 CONT Note that there's a controversy over whether Yehiel of Paris died in Acre in 1268, or whether he returned to France. There is a tombstone fragment (photo in the source linked below) from Paris (circa early 1300s) that bears his na
2 CONC me. If this is indeed his tombstone (and the 1292 tax roll suggests this), he must have been around 100 years old when he died. He was already the Rosh Yeshiva in Paris in 1225!
2 CONT
2 CONT The Hebrew version of the wiki page provides more genealogical details: [https://he.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D7%99%D7%97%D7%99%D7%90%D7%9C_%D7%9E%D7%A4%D7%A8%D7%99%D7%96 Hebrew wiki page]. It confirms that he was a Levite, that he had 
2 CONC a son Yosef (known as the "שיר דילשוש", who is buried in Carmel), as well as giving the names of two son-in-laws [https://he.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D7%99%D7%A6%D7%97%D7%A7_%D7%9E%D7%A7%D7%95%D7%A8%D7%91%D7%99%D7%9C Yitzkhak of Corbei
2 CONC lle] (wife's name not mentioned, but most likely Florion based on context) and [https://he.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D7%9E%D7%A8%D7%93%D7%9B%D7%99_%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%9C Mordechai] (wife: Zelda).
2 CONT
2 CONT Note that the ancestry tree is likely wrong. There is a different family from Cologne who moved to Toledo with alternating names of Asher and Yehiel. It looks like it has been conflated with the family from Paris. See: https://en.
2 CONC wikipedia.org/wiki/Asher_ben_Jehiel for details on the Cologne family.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Primary sources for Yehiel are listed in this paper: https://hal.archives-ouvertes.fr/hal-03331538/document
2 CONT
2 CONT Data in the above comes from a combination of tax rolls and cemetary records from Paris, France in the 1200s.
2 CONT
2 CONT Date: 1292<br />
2 CONT Name: Vivant de Miauz<br />
2 CONT Family details: Sarre la mirgesse his wife and his household ―sa mesnie‖, Florion his widowed daughter<br />
2 CONT Street: L‘Atacherie<br />
2 CONT From: Meaux (Seine-et Marne)<br />
2 CONT Taxes: 10s 
2 CONT
2 CONT Based on the above, his wife, Sarre, was a physician.
