1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Mattithiah ben Yosef''' "The Provencal" (of Provence)
2 CONT
2 CONT Chief rabbi of Paris and of France from 1360 to 1385; son of Joseph ben Johanan of Treves, rabbi of Marseilles; pupil of Perez b. Isaac ha-Kohen and of Nissim b. Reuben of Gerona.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1360 King Charles V. appointed him chief rabbi of the community of Paris and of all the newly organised communities of France, exempting him and '''Manecier of Vesoul''' from wearing the Jewish badge.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mattithiah founded a rabbinical school at Paris which soon attracted many pupils, eight of whom were called to various communities. He is probably identical with Mattithiah Treves (the author of MS. No. 676, folio 147, containing 
2 CONC a responsum, in the Paris Bibliothèque Nationale) and with Mattithiah "the Frank" (author of a methodological treatise on the Talmud).
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaac ben Sheshet (Responsa, No. 271) applies to him the title of "Even Boḥan" ("touchstone"), a term which has been held to imply that he composed a work bearing this name (Shabbethai Bass, "Sifte Yeshenim," x., No. 9). Zunz ("Li
2 CONC teraturgesch.") mentions a liturgical poet by the name of Mattithiah ben Joseph "the administrator" ("ha-parnes"), but this latter epithet can apply neither to Mattithiah ben Joseph nor to his father.
2 CONT
2 CONT Read more: http://www.jewishencyclopedia.com/view.jsp?artid=272&letter=M#ixzz0wz8vTlu6
2 CONT
2 CONT né en 1320 pour Judith Nathan?
2 CONT
2 CONT décédé en 1385?
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Asher אשר Klein קליין''' has sent '''Yigal''' a message (May 31, 2011), 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr Matityahu Ashkenazi Treves (b. 1325, d. 1385).
2 CONT
2 CONT Matityahu Ashkenazi Treves (son of Joseph Ashkenazi Treves) was born 1325, and died 1385 in Paris France.  He married (2) Daughter Spira.
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Matityahu Ashkenazi Treves: Died 2: 1385
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Matityahu Ashkenazi Treves are: 
2 CONT
2 CONT +Hana Vergentlin Treves, b. 1340.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Matityahu Ashkenazi Treves and Daughter Spira are: 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Abraham Treves.'''  + Yochanan Treves, b., Troyes France, d. 1429, Worms Germany.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Joseph Treves, d. 1429, Italy.''' + Daughter Treves, b. 1370. 
2 CONT  http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/r/u/b/Leon-Rubinstein/WEBSITE-0001/UHP-1575.html
2 CONT
2 CONT See:  http://trees.ancestry.com/tree/25067072/person/12113235149
2 CONT
2 CONT R. Mattatiahu lived as Chief Rabbi in Paris and was a man of great authority.  His daughter, wife of R. Samuel Spira, became the mother of R. Solomon Spira, 1350.  He was the father of Miriam, who was married to Rabbi Jechiel ben 
2 CONC Jechiel of Erfurt (Germany).  (Day of death 13th of Elul 1328)
