1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Uncle and teacher of https://www.geni.com/people/Rabbi-Yisrael-Isserlin-The-Terumas-Hadeshen/6000000000348861209. Normally assumed to be the brother of Yisrael's mother - https://www.geni.com/people/Breina-Brendel/
2 CONC 4110493451070022159. Some have gone so far to attach the suffix 'Blumelin' to Yisrael's mother. However there is no evidence to confirm this. This assumption is likely based on the fact they were both burned at the stake in Neusta
2 CONC dt. However, such reasoning is obviously flawed. Countless Jews were killed in those massacres and there is no proof they were even killed on the same day. It is more likely that https://www.geni.com/people/R-Aron-Bluemlein-of-Kre
2 CONC ms/6000000000348861312 was in fact a brother of https://www.geni.com/people/Rabbi-Petatiah/4110493404380027586, Yisrael's father. This is based on 2 arguments. 1) Yisrael's paternal family was a Rabbinic one from Krems, the town w
2 CONC here Aron lived and taught. 2) There is record of a Rabbi of the period known as Aron son of Hantchel. Hantchel was the name of Yisrael's paternal grandfather. One may also point out that after Yisrael's father's early death, Yisr
2 CONC ael was raised by Rabbi Aron. Whilst none of these arguments are 'watertight' the current Geni tree shows this as the route, as it seems the '''more''' likely of the two options.
