1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Used to teach students Torah while sitting behind a curtain.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Jewish Life in the Middle Ages"
2 CONT
2 CONT by Israel Abrahams  p. 343 - 344
2 CONT
2 CONT http://books.google.com/books?id=0RIqAAAAYAAJ&printsec=frontcover&dq=%22Jewish+Life+in+the+Middle+Ages%22+by+Israel+Abrahams&source=bl&ots=E6U-vLhB3M&sig=D7PLafwf09cw4-ylFJEUuEWIKks&hl=en&ei=G0ttTKSgNIP-8AbY853CDA&sa=X&oi=book_res
2 CONC ult&ct=result&resnum=1&ved=0CBIQ6AEwAA#v=onepage&q&f=false
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Miriam was the daughter of R' SOLOMON SPIRA and a Female TREVES.
2 CONT
2 CONT Female TREVES was the daughter of R' MATISYAHU TREVES (1325-1385), who was AV BAIS DIN of the town he lived in.
2 CONT
2 CONT R' MATISYAHU was the son of YOSEF TREVES (born 1305), known as "YOSEF TREVES THE GREAT." Yosef was AV BAIS DIN in Marseilles, Paris. Yosef's father was
2 CONT
2 CONT YOCHANAN TREVES ASHKENAZI.
2 CONT
2 CONT YOCHANAN'S father was
2 CONT
2 CONT ABRAHAM TREVES.
2 CONT
2 CONT Four generations later was SHLOMO YITZCHAKI, known as the famous RASHI (1040-1105).
2 CONT
2 CONT Continuing further back are: YOCHANAN HASANDLER, GAMLIEL HAZAKAIN, SHIMON HANASI, and HILLEL HAZAKAIN. The NODA B'YEHUDA traced his roots all the way back to KING DAVID - DAVID HAMELECH who reigned asKing of ISRAEL over 2000 years
2 CONC  ago.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://www.maxpages.com/nodabyehuda/Yechiel_Luria_d1470
2 CONT
