1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Itinerant Rabbi in Ferrara, Siena, Sabbionetta, Viadana, Bologna, Venice, Padua, Modena, and Ancona. Served as "private" rabbi in houses of rich bankers. Author of Kimha Deavishona (Bologna 1540-41). from Shlomo Si
2 CONC monsohn, History of the Jews in the Duchy of Mantua, p736, Tel-Aviv University, 1977
1 FAMC @F6000000000348912259@
1 FAMS @F6000000187287928833@
1 RFN geni:6000000000348881245
1 SUBM @S4743895211280029291@
1 NOTE My 2nd cousin 14 times removed.
2 CONT
2 CONT He studied in Ferrara, Italy, where he became a member of the beth din. For many years, he wandered in northern and central Italy, working as rabbi and religious teacher. For a number of years he lived in the home of Ishmael Rieti
2 CONC  in Siena acting as his private tutor. He then lived in Sabbioneta and Bologna, Italy, where he apparently worked in the Hebrew press. Treves was a scholar and publisher, writing responsa and a well-known commentary on the festiva
2 CONC l prayer book according to the Roman rite.
