1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Parnass (Head) of Jewish community in Krakow. Built a synagogue in honor of his son (Rema/Remuh Synagogue) in the Kazimierz area in Krakow in 1553.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to The Lurie Legacy, The House of Davidic Royal Descent by Neil Rosenstein Israel (Isarel Lazers) and Dina Malka Had Four Sons and Three Daughters
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 1567.  Eminent Talmudic scholar and director of the Jewish community in Krakow.
2 CONT
2 CONT Israel (known as Isserl), was a prominent talmudist and independently wealthy, who had probably headed the community of Krakow.
2 CONT
2 CONT His son Moshe was called Isserles in a patronymic way, at the time were surnames were inexistent.
