1 OCCU Printer
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://www.zeeuwseankers.nl/verhaal/portugese-joden-in-zeeland His father is seen as the Founder of Judaism in England by the english jews.]
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Menasseh_Ben_Israel
2 CONT
2 CONT Menasseh's wife, Rachel, was a granddaughter of the Abarbanel. Menasseh had three children by her. Menasseh's wife was, according to family legend, a descendant of King David, and he was proud of his children's Davidic ancestry.
2 CONT
2 CONT Both of Menasseh's sons predeceased their father.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Menasseh's eldest son was Samuel Abarbanel Soeiro, also known as Samuel Ben Israel, who worked as a printer and assisted his father with matters in England. He died in 1657.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Menasseh's son, Joseph, died at age 20, in 1650, on a disastrous business trip to Poland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Menasseh also had a daughter, Gracia, born 1628, who married Samuel Abarbanel Barboza in 1646, and died in 1690.
