1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From David Gans, Zemach David:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1576/77   Rabbi Natan of Grodno, son of my uncle, Shimshon Spira z"l......... Natan died in 5337, and he left two sons who were great in Torah: r' Isaac who was Rosh Y. in Kabla (?) and r' Issachar, who was Rosh Y. in Pinsk. And a
2 CONC t this time he (Issachar) is Rosh Y. & AB"D in Worms [Worms Mem. p.5 and see his daughter Epidat wrm-3021 – her name is really Gelle, per Gruene Buch]
2 CONT
2 CONT Was known as Hagaaon Rabbi Natan-Neta from Horodna. Writer of "Mavoh Shearim".
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Samson Spira: rabbi at Grodno; died 1577.   He wrote a super commentary on the commentaries of Rashi and Elijah Mizrahi under the title of "Imre Shefer", and a commentary on the Penateuch, published by his son Isaac (Lubin,
2 CONC  1586 [1597]), and at the request of his pupils "Mevo She'Arim" (Lublin nd, Jessnitz 1724), a commentary on Isaac Duran's "Sha'are Durah". 
2 CONT
2 CONT Nathan That left two sons:  Isaac and Israel Issachar. The Zohar was edited not by him, but by Natan ben Isaac Spira (Lublin, 1624]). [http://www.jewishencyclopedia.com/articles/13965-spira-spiro  ''Source]
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>><nowiki>-----------------------------</nowiki>
2 CONT
2 CONT *[http://wiki.geni.com/index.php/Jewish_Dynasties  ''Jewish Dynasties]
2 CONT
2 CONT See also Fig. 7 in [http://www.surnamedna.com/?articles=y-dna-of-the-savran-bendery-chassidic-dynasty#ref23 Y-DNA Genetic Signature of the Savran-Bendery Chassidic Dynasty]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Son of Samson Spira; rabbi at Grodno; died 1577. He wrote a supercommentary on the commentaries of Rashi and Elijah Mizraḥi under the title "Imre Shefer," and a commentary on the Pentateuch, published by his son Isaac (Lublin, 158
2 CONC 6 [1597]), and at the request of his pupils "Mebo She'arim" (Lublin, n.d.; Jessnitz, 1724), a commentary on Isaac Duran's "Sha'are Durah." The Zohar was edited not by him, as Fürst and others think, but by Nathan b. Isaac Spira (L
2 CONC ublin, 1624). Nathan Nata left two sons: Isaac (No. 12) and Israel Issachar (No. 14).
2 CONT
2 CONT Bibliography:
2 CONT David Gans, Ẓemaḥ Dawid, ed. Offenbach, p. 30a; Jehiel Heilprin, Seder ha-Dorot, ed. Warsaw, i 248; Azulai, l.c. i. 148; De Rossi-Hamberger, l.c. p. 301; Fuenn, l.c. p. 55; Fürst, l.c. iii. 373; Zedner, Cat. Hebr. Books Brit. Mus.
2 CONC  p. 609.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT From "Tiferes Aryeh"
2 CONT
2 CONT AB"D Horadna and Pozna
2 CONT
2 CONT Author of "Mevoh Shearim"
