1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.aspx?req=30378&st=&pgnum=17
2 CONT
2 CONT Meshullam Solomon Fischhof-Auerbach, occupied such an eminent position in the community of Vienna that he married Miriam, the daughter of a well-known rabbi and physician Leo Lucerna (Judah Löb Ma'or-ḳaṭon). She died July 29, 1654
2 CONC  (Frankl, "Inschriften," No. 202). In his old age it was his misfortune to be driven from Vienna and exiled (1670) with his coreligionists. Before his death (1677) he had the satisfaction of seeing his sons occupy honorable positi
2 CONC ons. Nearly twenty years before, his son Menahem Mendel Auerbach was called as rabbi to Reussnitz, Moravia, after having officiated as assessor to the rabbinate at Cracow. The pupil of such men as Lipmann Heller, Joel Särkes, Josh
2 CONC ua b. Joseph, at the Talmud school in Cracow, Menahem Mendel attained such a reputation as a Talmudic authority that the rabbis of large foreign communities submitted difficult questions to him for decision.
2 CONT
2 CONT from: http://www.jewishencyclopedia.com/view.jsp?artid=2108&letter=A
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Die Grabschriften des Alten Judenfriedhofes in Wein" Band I by Dr. Bernhard Wachstein- pg. 329, 415
