3 CTRY Germany
1 OCCU Chief Rabbi of Hamburg; ABD of of the tri-communities of Altona, Hamburg and Wandsbeck., Rabbi, author of "Knesset Jecheskiel", Cheif Rabbi of Sislowitz, Chief Rabbi, Hamburg, ABD Hamburg, Chief rabbi of Altona and Hamburg, author
2 CONC  of "Kneset Yehezkel"
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Born 1668 or 1669, Ezekiel himself was uncertain of the fact. He grew up in Brest where he studied under R. Mordecai Susskind,son of R. Moses Rothenberg who lived there until about 1691. He was first Av Beth Din of
2 CONC  the toen on Zdzieciol (Zitel) then Av Beth Din Raseiniai. In 1707 he was called to Keidaniai and to Altona in 1714 where he served the community for 35 years until his death. The community at this time was under Danish rule.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ezekiel married Esther , daughter of R. Solomon Zalman, who was the son of R. Joel of Brest (the grandson of R. Joel Sirkes called the BaCh). Ester died in 1748 and was buried in the Koningstrasse Cemetry, Altone (Tombstone no 307
2 CONC 2).
2 CONT
2 CONT The Chief Rabbi (Av Beth Din or ABD) of Keidaniai, until 1714, was Rabbi Ezekiel Katzenellenpogen (a descendant through the female line who had adopted the name from the Katzenellenbogen male line.)[1] He then became Av Beth Din o
2 CONC f the famous triple community of Altona-Hamburg-Wansdbeck where he remained until his death in 1749.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in Altona July 9th (23rd Tammuz) 1749.  Buried next to his wife. Tombstone 3073.
2 CONT
2 CONT His son R’ David succeeded him in 1714 as ABD Keidaniai, and he was succeeded by his son, R’ Meshullam Zalman ABD Keidaniai.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Source=
2 CONT
2 CONT Author of "Kenesset Yezekiel"
2 CONT Mayim Yechezkiel (published 1786) Tefillot le-Yartzheit (published 1727) Tzava'at Yechezkiel  - His Ethical Will (published 1750, and again in 1871 by a descendant) Me'orer Zikkaron (published 1727) He wrote numerous approbations
2 CONT
2 CONT Chief Rabbi of Beth Din of Hamburg
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile photo:  The Great Synagogue of Altonahttp://www.biblesearchers.com/yahshua/beithillel/emden.shtml
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://he.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D7%99%D7%97%D7%96%D7%A7%D7%90%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%A6%D7%99%D7%A0%D7%90%D7%9C%D7%A4%D7%95%D7%92%D7%99%D7%9F עברית]
2 CONT
2 CONT The Unbroken Chain, Neil Rosenstein, 1990, page 584, G7.2
2 CONT
