1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [http://www.davidicdynasty.org/shapiro_art.php     '''SPIRA Family Tree]
2 CONT #(1) Shmuel SPIRA (born about 1345) , married to Vergentlin TREVES, a daughter of the Rashi-descendant # Mattitjahu Treves (see RASHI descendants). Their son was R. Shlomo SPIRA. 
2 CONT # (2) R. Shlomo SPIRA's son was R. Peretz SPIRA. 
2 CONT # (3) Rabbi Peretz SPIRA was rabbi in Konstanz, Germany. His son was Rabbi Nathan Nata SPIRA. 
2 CONT # (4) Rabbi Nathan Nata SPIRA was rabbi in Posen. His son was Rabbi Shimshon SPIRA. 
2 CONT # (5) Rabbi Shimshon SPIRA was also rabbi in Posen. His children:
2 CONT * 	•	(6a) Rabbi Nathan Nata SPIRA (died in 1577), rabbi in Grodno, author of Mevo Shearim and Imrei Shefer, grandfather of R. Nathan Nata SPIRA (1585 - 1633, author of Megaleh Amukot) 
2 CONT * 	•	(6b) Rabbi Yechiel Michel SPIRA (born about 1530, rabbi in Posen). Warning: This conflicts with information from Lawrence WEINBERG devoutbokononist@gmail.com who has two sources claiming Yechiel Michel SPIRA's father was Yose
2 CONC f Yerushalmi SPIRA.
2 CONT >>* 	◦	(7a) '''Rabbi Chaim SPIRA, Posen'''
2 CONT >>* 	◦	(7b) R. Wolf Elabes Spira (died in Prag).
2 CONT >>>>>* 	▪	Rabbi Aaron Shimon SPIRA, chief-rabbi in Prague
2 CONT >>>>>* 	▪	Ascher Anschel SPIRA
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.davidicdynasty.org/shapiro_art.php  '''The Shapiro Family Tree]  
