2 NOTE Our teacher the Maharsha, of blessed memory, was the father-in-law of the sharp and righteous gaon R. Moshe, son of the gaon R. Yitzchak, of blessed memory. And the aforementioned R. Yitzchak was the son-in-law of the gaon R. Simc
3 CONC ha Bunim, head of the rabbinical court of the holy community of Kraków, [who was] son-in-law of the rabbi, gaon, and righteous one R. Moshe Isserles [the Rema], of blessed memory, author of the Mappah.
3 CONT
3 CONT The aforementioned R. Moshe son of R. Yitzchak was head of the rabbinical court of the holy community of Lublin, and he was the author of the Mahadura Batra on the Maharsha. His son-in-law was the rabbi and gaon R. Avraham Finges,
3 CONC  of blessed memory.
3 CONT
3 CONT The son of R. Avraham was the great rabbi R. Yosef, the Chasid of Keidan [Kėdainiai]. The son of R. Yosef was the rabbi, gaon, and righteous one R. Kalman, head of the rabbinical court of the holy community of Pinsk. The son of R.
3 CONC  Kalman was the rabbi, gaon, and righteous one R. Leib, of blessed memory, and his wife was the renowned righteous woman Mrs. Gittel, of blessed memory, daughter of the rabbi and gaon R. Pinchas Shmeringer, of blessed memory, and 
3 CONC sister of the rabbi and gaon R. Moshe, of blessed memory, head of the rabbinical court of the holy community of Lusk [Lutsk].
3 CONT
3 CONT The wife of R. Pinchas Shmeringer was the daughter of the gaon R. Shmuel, son of the rabbi R. Elkanah, of blessed memory, head of the rabbinical court of the holy community of Bitshov(?), author of the responsa volume Stam Shmuel;
3 CONC  and he was a native of Altona. He was the father of the rabbi and gaon, our teacher R. Pesach, of blessed memory, author of the book Kemach Pesach — resolutions of difficulties in the words of Rashi and Tosafot in the places wher
3 CONC e the Maharsha raises objections against them.
3 CONT
3 CONT The rabbi, gaon, and righteous one R. Leib, of blessed memory, had three sons. The first was the rabbi, gaon, and righteous one R. Shmuel, of blessed memory, head of the rabbinical court of the holy communities of Antopol, Karlin,
3 CONC  and Pinsk
