2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT From Chenowicz, Moshe. Rabbis & Notables of Wlodimierz, in Wladimir Wolynsk: in memory of the Jewish community, 1962:
2 CONT
2 CONT Rabbi Ephraim Naftali son of Rabbi Joseph Jonah
2 CONT
2 CONT In those days the yeshiva in Ludmir was able to appoint Rabbi Ephraim Naftali son of Rabbi Joseph Jonah....
2 CONT
2 CONT Specific details about this head of the Ludmir yeshiva have not survived. We only know that before Ludmir he was a head of yeshiva in Brisk, Lithuania (Brest, Belarus today).[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Rabbi Ephraim Naftali died 25 Tammuz 1622 in Ludmir....
2 CONT
2 CONT [4] The Rabbi and head of the rabbinic court there at that time was his father-in-law Rabbi Jakob, son of Moshe Halevi, son-in-law of the Maharam of Padua, grandfather of the officer and emissary Saul Wahl of Brisk, Lithuania (Bre
2 CONC st, Belarus today), about whom the famous legend is told of his reigning as King of Poland for one day.
