1 NAME Aharon Menachem /HaCohen/
2 GIVN Aharon Menachem
2 SURN HaCohen
2 _MARNM HaCohen
1 SEX M
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Source: Elef Margaliot by Rabbi Meir Wunder, Page 493, Entry 710 (1993)
2 CONT
2 CONT       **************************************
2 CONT
2 CONT According to data reported by https://www.geni.com/people/Rabbi-Dr-J-Simcha-Cohen/6000000002702955788:
2 CONT
2 CONT "HaRav HaGaon R. Shmuel HaKohen, my paternal grandfather, was seriously concerned with the genealogical roots of the family. In the introduction to his classic s'farim, he delineated direct relationships to various sages, spanning
2 CONC  approximately 500 years of Jewish life. In addition he acquired the services of HaRav R. Avraham I'Tigna from Dukla, Galicia, a genealogical scholar and author of "Shem HaG'dolim" vol. III to research the family lineage. The resu
2 CONC lts, entitled "Tipheret Avot" were published in "M'danai Shmuel" on Laws of Pesach." (SOURCE: Sh'Tar Yichus- L'Zecher Nishmot, document in the file entitled 'Burstein Family History, circa 1981' within the "Russler and Burstein fa
2 CONC mily papers, 1930-1992” collection held by the Bienecke Library of Yale University under call number: YCAL MSS 1117 Box 9).
2 CONT
2 CONT In this document there is the following entry for Aharon Menachem HaCohen father of Shalom Shachna Kahana RaSHaCH of Cracow
2 CONT
2 CONT "HaGaon R. Aharon Menchem Katz (1835)
2 CONT (Called R. Mendel, R. Zalman Hazzan)
2 CONT (The Tipheret Avot, published in the M'danai Shmuel, contends
2 CONT that R. Aharon Menachem was the grandson of R. Aaron Moshe
2 CONT (d. 9 Adar 1616) who was the son of
2 CONT HaRav HaGaon R. Yosef Katz"
2 CONT [Note: the latter is She'erit Yosef)
2 CONT
2 CONT This is further corroborated in the Elef Margoliot # 711 (which is posted to that profile).
2 CONT
2 CONT However, there is no source I have seen suggesting who the father of Aharon Menachem was nor that it was Yosef Yehuda Leyb. Presumably, the fact that Wunder, although including Yosef Yehuda as a son of Aharon Moshe in entry # 711,
2 CONC  DOES NOT CLAIM that Yosef was the father of Aharon Menachem in either # 711 or # 710, but only that Aharon Menachem was the grandson of Aharon Moshe, indicates that Wunder had no reason to believe that Aharon Menachem was the son
2 CONC  of Yosef Yehuda Leyb.
