1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT "Menahem Mendel ben Meshullam Auerbach (died July 8, 1689) (Hebrew: מנחם מענדל אויערבאך) was an Austrian rabbi, banker, and commentator born in Vienna at the beginning of the 17th century. He was descended from the well-known Auer
2 CONC bach-Fischhof family, both his father, Meshullam Solomon, and his maternal grandfather, Rabbi Judah Loeb Rofe, being members of the Vienna Ghetto."
2 CONT
2 CONT ======================================================================================
2 CONT
2 CONT Links:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Menahem_Mendel_Auerbach
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.jewishencyclopedia.com/articles/2124-auerbach-menahem-mendel-ben-meshullam-solomon
2 CONT
2 CONT See (in Hebrew) page 19 at:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://hebrewbooks.org/26471
2 CONT
2 CONT "Die Grabschriften des Alten Judenfriedhofes in Wien" Band I, by Dr. Bernhard Wachstein-pg. 329 (no. 429)
2 CONT
2 CONT  autor of "Atheret Zkenim"
2 CONT ----
