2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT From the JewishEncyclopedia.com (1906):
2 CONT
2 CONT Nathan Nata Spira
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Solomon Spira and grandson of Nathan Nata Spira; born about 1584; died July 20, 1633.
2 CONT In 1617 he was called to the rabbinate of Cracow, where, being well-to-do, he refused to accept a salary.
2 CONT He was gifted with an extraordinary memory, and devoted much time to the study of the Cabala. He wrote a cabalistic commentary on the prayer of Moses in Deut. iii. 24, and two prayers, under the title "Megalleh 'Amuḳḳot" (Cracow, 
2 CONC 1637; Fürth, 1691). He published also novellæ to Alfasi's work which were printed with it (Amsterdam, 1720).
2 CONT
2 CONT Bibliography
2 CONT
2 CONT Azulai, l.c. i. 148; De Rossi-Hamberger, l.c. p. 301; Steinschneider, l.c. col. 2049; Zunz, Monatstage, p. 41; Zedner, l.c. p. 610; I. M. Zunz, 'Ir ha-Ẓedeḳ, pp. 52, 176 (contains Spira's epitaph).
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT From the Yivo Encyclopedia of Jews in Eastern Europe:
