2 DATE 1713
2 ADDR
3 CITY Kraków
3 STAE Lillpolen
3 CTRY Poland
1 OCCU Chief Rabbi, Rabbi/Judge
1 TITL Rabbi
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Chief Rabbi of Przemysl and Krakow (until 1713). Son of R. Shmelke Zak. Son-in-law of the Meginei Shlomo. See:  [http://hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.aspx?req=1203&st=&pgnum=203] [https://beta.hebrewbooks.org/reader/rea
2 CONC der.aspx?sfid=59815#p=59&fitMode=fitwidth&hlts=&ocr=%u05DE%u05D0%u05D9%u05E8%20%u05D6%22%u05E7] [http://hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.aspx?req=15241&st=&pgnum=6] [https://www.jewishgen.org/Yizkor/przemysl/prz037.html '''RABBI YITZCHAK 
2 CONC IZAK'''] [https://kehilalinks.jewishgen.org/Krakow/kra_rabbis.htm]
2 CONT
2 CONT Rabbi Isaac ABD Cracow was the son–in–law of his predecessor, the “Pnei Yehoshua”. According to Dr. Gelernter, who does not bring a source to support his opinion, he was the son of Rabbi Shmuel Szmelka, and the father of the Gaon 
2 CONC Rabbi Yehuda Leib, the head of the rabbinical court and the Yeshiva of Krakow, who served in Przemysl as a rabbinical judge and rabbi. However, it still remains in doubt if he actually served as the head of the rabbinical court in
2 CONC  Przemysl, but it does seem that prior to this he was the rabbi in a different city, and therefore earned this title as well. Professor Schorr includes him in the list of rabbis of Przemysl without any qualification. We do not kno
2 CONC w the dates of his tenure, but it is clear that Rabbi Menachem Mendel who followed him ascended the rabbinical seat of Przemysl in the year 5402 (1642). 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Who was his father?
2 CONT * According to the testimony of his descendants (https://www.geni.com/people/R-Joshua-Wallerstein-A-B-D-Rzeszow/6000000002764525778 and https://www.geni.com/people/Rabbi-Shmelke-Licht-ABD-Bumsla/6000000077585091883?through=6000000
2 CONC 077584648301), Yitzchak Isaac was the son of https://www.geni.com/people/R-Shmuel-Shmeilke-Zak-Zera-Kodesh/6000000000037116449?through=5202804771060053620. It should be noted that Rabbi Shmuel Shmelke Zak was an honored colleague 
2 CONC of the Meginei Shlomo, who was incidentally Yitzchak Isaac's father-in-law . 
2 CONT * According to some, Yitzchak Isaac was a son of https://www.geni.com/people/R-Shmuel-Zvi-Hirsch-Naftali-Sirkis-Yaffe-Pi%C5%84cz%C3%B3w-Rebbe/6000000000249464283. Meir Wunder says this is wrong.
2 CONT * According to others, Yitzchok Isaac was a son of https://www.geni.com/people/Rabbi-Aryeh-Yehuda-Leib-Sirkis-Yaffe-Shaagat-Arye-Kol-Shakhal/6000000000803308061
2 CONT
