2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Simcha_Rappaport '''Simcha Rappaport'''] Wikipedia
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Rabbi Simcha Hagadol HaKohen Rappaport''' (Hebrew: שמחה הכהן ראפאפארט; b. 1650 - August 4, 1718) was a 17th-century Ukrainian rabbi and progenitor of the Rappaport rabbinic dynasties. Born in about 1650 in L'viv, Ukraine. His f
2 CONC ather, Rabbi Nachman of Belz was a minor rabbi and a descendant of Rashi through his mother. In his early years Rabbi Rappaport studied in L'viv. In 1688 he was appointed the Chief Rabbi of Horodna. He was later appointed to be Av
2 CONC  Bris Din of Levov, although he died on the way there on August 4, 1718 in Szczebrzeszyn. The Soloveitchik dynasty claims Rabbi Rappaport as a notable ancestor and progenitor.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ********************************************************************
2 CONT
2 CONT The death date but not sure was:
2 CONT
2 CONT July 4, 1717
2 CONT
2 CONT Ori modified to:
2 CONT
2 CONT נסתלק ביום ז׳ אב שנת תע״ח
2 CONT
2 CONT which is Aug 4th 1718 based on the below grave story
2 CONT
2 CONT See Grave story here
2 CONT
2 CONT הגאון מוה' שמחה הכהן ראפפורט
2 CONT
2 CONT בשנת תע"ח לאחר
2 CONT פטירת הגאון מאוה"ג חכם צבי ז"ל בלבוב ביום ב׳ דר"ח אייר תע"ח לפ"ק קראו ראשי
2 CONT ומנהיגי העדה דשם את הגאון רבינו שמחה הכהן הנ"ל לבוא אליהם לכהן פאר בעדתם,
2 CONT ולהיות אב"ד ור"מ בק"ק לבוב והגליל, למלאות מקום הגאון חכם צבי ז"ל, והגאון
2 CONT מוה' שמחה קבל המשרה הנכבדה הזאת, כי חפץ לשבת על כסא אבי אמו הגאון
2 CONT מוה' יוסף במוה' אליקים געץ ז"ל שהי' מקודם אב"ד בלבוב ויצא הגאון מעירנו וילך
2 CONT לבובה קרית משוש תפארתו ״ אבל לדאבון נפשו לא נהקיימה מחשבתו כי חלה באם
2 CONT הדרך ונפטר והלך לעולמו בעיר שעברשין ביום ז' אב תע"ח לפ"ק
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.yiddishworld.com/forum/viewtopic.php?f=31&t=9986
2 CONT
2 CONT Became Rabbi of Horodna in 1688 http://www.hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.aspx?req=36783&pgnum=66
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.asp ... 3&pgnum=66
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Mentioned in the book
2 CONT
2 CONT See Here
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.hebrewbooks.org/36875
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Ancestor of the Soloveitchik dynasty.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Soloveitchik family includes many significant rabbinical forebears, most notably Rabbi Chaim Volozhiner, famed Talmudist and founder of the Volozhin yeshiva.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rabbi Chaim Volozhiner ( 1749-1821), was a student of the Vilna Gaon, and thus some students of Brisk talk of a line of tradition extending "from Moses at Sinai, to Joshua, to the Elders ... to the Vilna Gaon, to Rabbi Chaim Voloz
2 CONC hiner, and then to the Soloveitchik dynasty."
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chaim_Soloveitchik (see bio)
2 CONT
2 CONT Most scholars, however, begin the Soloveitchik dynasty with Rabbi Joseph Dov (HaLevi) Soloveitchik known as the Beis HaLevi (see below), as he was the first rabbi of Brisk surnamed Soloveitchik. More significantly, the "Brisker st
2 CONC yle" described below can already be found to some degree in the Beis HaLevi's works, which is not the case for earlier ancestors.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yosef_Dov_Soloveitchik_(Beis_Halevi) (see bio)
2 CONT
2 CONT All members of the Soloveitchik family are descended from the tribe of Levi and thus sometimes go by the descriptor "HaLevi".
2 CONT
2 CONT The surname "Soloveitchik", in fact, is Polish for "nightingale"; it was chosen by the family because the primary duty of the Levites in the Temple in Jerusalem was singing. (Note that the surname "Soloveitchik" can be spelled eit
2 CONC her as presented, or as "Soloveichik", without the "t".
2 CONT
2 CONT http://wiki.geni.com/index.php/Jewish_Dynasties
2 CONT
2 CONT 11/5/10-Ori:
2 CONT
2 CONT See http://rapaport-heb.blogspot.com/
2 CONT
2 CONT I corrected the name Rapoport to Rappaport
2 CONT
2 CONT This fits theHebrew spelling and the explanation in the above site
2 CONT
2 CONT =======================
