1 TITL Rabbi
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} R. Izchak (born ca. 1520) was the son of R. Dovid. Two of his children are known; his son Yakov published באר מים חיים, 1616. His daughter Esther was the wife of R. Meir b. Gedalya, the famous Maharam Lublin. Rabbi
2 CONC  Izchak was Rav in Kremnitz and is said to have taken the position of Rabbi in Cracow after the passing of the Remo in 1572. He was a founder member of the Vaad Arba Arazot. He died in 1582, his wife Beila died in 1600. His son la
2 CONC ments that the writings and correspondence of his father were lost, and the only trace of his literary status is found in a few scattered ספרים (תשובות הב"ח 73, נתיבות עולם Prague 1596, נתיב הלשון ט ) and the תשובות of his son in 
2 CONC law, Rav Meir (1558-1616), who signs many times חתן המלך מו"ר יצחק הכהן שפירא. ) עיר הצדק, Lemberg 1874, chapter 3, also notes 11 and footnote 3, addenda).
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Rosh Yeshiva and Dayan at Cracov: Jacobi Papers: Volume 4, p. 188, 16.3m
2 CONT Father in Law of Maharam of Lublin: Jacobi Papers: Volume 4, p. 210, 15.4
