1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Attention :
2 CONT
2 CONT Rabbi Meir Zak serait né 4 ans avant sa mère Dinah
2 CONT
2 CONT Rabbi Meir Zak would have been born 4 years before his mother Dinah    (JDGH)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT From Kaganoff, Benzion C. Jewish Surnames Through the Ages: An Etymological History. Commmentary, September 1, 1956:
2 CONT
2 CONT Zak comes from Zera K'doshim = "descendants of the martyrs."
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT From Geni.com:
2 CONT
2 CONT Adopted the surname Zak after the martyrdom of his brother Rabbi Mordechai Avdek Lublin.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family name ZK - the initials of Zera Kadosh (seed of saints) - who gave their lives for Kiddush Hashem as stated in the book Shalshelet Zahav page 79.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Ga'on Rabbi Meir Zak, Av Beit Din of Lvov, was a disciple of the Maharal of Lublin.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to family tradition, he is descended from the Baal Turim.
2 CONT
2 CONT See:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.aspx?req=48011&st=&pgnum=697&hilite=
2 CONT
2 CONT http://hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.aspx?req=3711&st=&pgnum=149&hilite=
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.aspx?req=10138&st=%D7%9E%D7%92%D7%99%D7%A0%D7%99+%D7%A9%D7%9C%D7%9E%D7%94&pgnum=64
2 CONT
2 CONT http://hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.aspx?req=29120&hilite=ad7f7712-155f-4d13-a6b6-1773f011fe45&st=%D7%90%D7%91%D7%A8%D7%94%D7%9D+%D7%96%22%D7%A7
2 CONT
2 CONT    *****************************
2 CONT
2 CONT "...Rabbi Menachem Nachum ben Israel Sak. He was doubtless the son of the martyr Rabbi Israel Sak, a nephew of Rabbi Meir Sak of Lemberg." Cullman, Peter Simonstein. History of the Jewish Community of Schneidemuhl: 1641 to the Hol
2 CONC ocaust. Avotaynu. Bergenfield, NJ 2006.p. 25.
