1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Also cf. various historical newspaper articles about Markus Benedikt (N.B. generally the name under which he was known at the time):
2 CONT
2 CONT e.g.
2 CONT
2 CONT ANNO, Allgemeine Zeitung des Judenthums. Ein unpartheiisches Organ für alles jüdisches Interesse in Betreff von Politik, Religion ..., 1862-06-17, Seite 5
2 CONT
2 CONT http://anno.onb.ac.at/cgi-content/anno?aid=azj&datum=18620617&seite=5&zoom=33&query=%22Benedict%2Bnikolsburg%22~9&ref=anno-search
2 CONT
2 CONT In which there are a few interesting details such as ...
2 CONT
2 CONT - Markus BENEDIKT's father is described as being a "Fleischhauer" - butcher - in Csurgó.
2 CONT
2 CONT - his maternal grandmother is described as a "poor widow" at the time he is sent to Nikolsburg as a five-year-old.
2 CONT
2 CONT - A rather confusing - erroneous in dates? - mention of his engagement and subsequent marriage to the daughter of Gumpel PROSSNITZ: "Im Jahre 1781(?) wurde er von Markburg nach Nikolsburg berufen, wo er sich mit der einzigen 14 jä
2 CONC hrigen Tochter des Gumpel Prossnitz verlobte. ... 1773 vollzog er seine Verehelichung ..."
2 CONT
2 CONT &
2 CONT
2 CONT ANNO, Die Neuzeit, 1901-02-08, Seite 4
2 CONT
2 CONT http://anno.onb.ac.at/cgi-content/anno?aid=neu&datum=19010208&seite=4&zoom=33&query=%22Benedict%2Bnikolsburg%22~9&ref=anno-search
2 CONT
2 CONT In which it is written: "Väterlicherseits stammte er von R. Zebi Hirsch, Verfasser der Responsen "Chacham Zebi" und mütterlicherseits von R. Naftali Kohn, Rabbiner in Frankfurt a. M. ab."
2 CONT
2 CONT Both his mother Fradl and maternal grandmother Rebekka are described as being very "devout". His maternal grandfather R. Aberl Benet is described as being a highly regarded Talmudist.
2 CONT
2 CONT etc. etc.
2 CONT
2 CONT (pip - Jan 2019)
2 CONT --------------------
