2 CONT H-K p.130	harabbanit Edel bt haGaon hagadol Abram Aschkenasi zTs”l AB”D dk”k Lvov {this is Abraham Aschkenasi 1578-1649 bn Moshe Heilbronn} e’ harosh Isaac Chajes j”Ts darschan  (Footnote: She died btw 1649 when Abram died and  16
2 CONC 87, when Isaac Chajes died) (2nd footnote: Abraham Aschkenasi Katzenellenbogen died in Iyar 1637 and was son-in-law of the Isaac Chajes darschan who was author of Pne Jitschak and Pakad Jitschak {i.e. the Isaac Chajes who had d. 1
2 CONC 615] and Abraham was the son of a brother of rav Isaac bn Moshe Katzenellenbogen of Neustaedtl as is written in his book, Moldot Jitschak, Prag 1622/23) [Special note: It is Abraham Aschkenasi Heilbronn who was AB”D in Lvov and wr
2 CONC ote Ahavat Zion, a super-commentary on Rashi, and died 1649. The other Abraham d.1637 at an old age, and was son of Joel Katzenellenbogen. In spite of the Lvov and Chajes connections of both Abrahams, Abraham Aschkenasi Heilbronn 
2 CONC is almost certainly Edel’s father]
