1 OCCU Rabbi, Cheif Rabbi of Brisk, Cheif Rabbi of Kowerki
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Succeeded his father Abraham as head of court in Brest Litovsk (Brisk)
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT rabbi of Brisk
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT He was rabbi of Brest-Litovsk and was in turn succeeded by his son Aryeh Löb Katzenellenbogen. A "hesped" or sermon preached on the occasion of Abraham's death is contained in Eliezer ha-Levi's "Reaḥ ha-Sadeh" (Shklov, 1795).
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Unbroken Chain p.585 G10.1 ____________________________________________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT born about 1750, succeeded his father as ABD of Brest Litovsk in 1804, married 1) Achsah, died in 1772, the daughter of R. Simha HaLevi, ABD Slonim, and 2) his niece, Bonah, daughter of R. Ezekiel Katenellenbogen, ABD Svisloch
2 CONT
2 CONT Unbroken Chain, 3rd edition, Volume 3, page 341
