1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Rabbi Elieser Shapiro was A.B.D. Lubetech, and descendants of the Rabbinical family of Spira / Shapiro.
2 CONT
2 CONT Gitel Shapiro, his daughter, was the second wife of Aryry Leib Shapiro.
2 CONT
2 CONT Aryey Leib Shapiro was the son of  R' Menachem Zundel Shapiro A.B.D. Ivenets (Eivenitz).  He died about 1783.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Source=
2 CONT
2 CONT The Unbroken Chain - Neil Rosenstein (1990) Volume 1, Chapter 11, page 133 G 13.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ר' מנחם זונדל לא היה בנו של ר' יצחק שפירא אלא בנו של ר' שלמה (לא ידוע שם משפחתו ויחוסו) כשמת ר' מנחם זונדל עבר בנו הילד אריה לייב לאבי אימו ר' אליעזר שפירא מלובאץ', שגידל אותו, ולכן גם הנכד, ר' אריה לייב, קרא לעצמו שפירא. אביו של 
2 CONC ר' אליעזר שפירא היה ר' אריה לייב שפירא מווילנה. אביו של ר' אריה לייב מווילנה היה ר' יצחק שפירא מדרוהוביץ אביו של ר' יצחק מדרוהוביץ היה ר' אליעזר שפירא ממינסק (על פי מאמרו של חוקר תולדות המשפחה ר' חיים קרלינסקי, ביטאון מוריה, שנה 1
2 CONC 3, גליון ג–ד ניסן תשמ"ד) NATANANSHIN@GMAIL.COM
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT 1784 Lubcha https://www.jewishgen.org/yizkor/lyubcha/lyu254.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Leizor the son of Leib, wife Dvora, daughter Ester, 2nd daughter Nechama
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.jewishgen.org/yizkor/Lyubcha/lyu079.html
2 CONT Details of Rabbi Eliezer Shapira's biography have not been preserved and the scant information that we have has come down to us indirectly from the identification of famous rabbis to the above-mentioned rabbi, who was a special de
2 CONC scendant of the Shapira family of Vilna-Lubtch.
2 CONT
2 CONT We know that R' Eliezer was a native of Vilna. His father, the Gaon R' Aryeh-Leib Shapira, 5461-5521(1701-1761) served as a scribe and judge in the rabbinical court in Vilna and acquired fame in the world of Torah as the author of
2 CONC  a two-part treatise, “Nachalat Ariel” (based on its plain meaning) and “Ma'on Arayot”, (based on argumentation) on the Talmud tractate, “Sofrim” (1732). He also wrote a book on the Torah “Kvutzat Kesef” (1742).
2 CONT
2 CONT It is impossible to determine exactly when R' Eliezer served as head of the rabbinical court in Lubtch. However, it was a long time after the term of office of R' Yosef-Moshe-Simcha HaCohen Rapoport, who is discussed above. We can
2 CONC  point out that R' Eliezer was famous in his time and was known by the great rabbis of Lithuania, many of whom were related to the rabbi who functioned in Lubtch, as we shall see further in this article.
2 CONT
2 CONT We don't know if R' Eliezer Shapira had any sons, but it is known that he had two daughters: one was married to R' Menachem-Zundel, head of the rabbinical court in Eibnitz, and the other was married to R' Chaim Epshtein from among
2 CONC  the notable families of Vilna, the “Jerusalem of Lithuania”. 
