1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Elijah Spira:
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Benjamin Wolf Spira; 
2 CONT
2 CONT Elijah Spira died at Prague April 14, 1712. He was rabbi at Tiktin, and afterward preacher and director of a large Talmudic academy at Prague. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He published "Eliyahu Zuṭa," a commentary on that part of Mordecai Jafe's "Lebush" relating to the Shulḥan 'Aruk, Oraḥ Ḥayyim (Prague, 1689, 1701). 
2 CONT
2 CONT His valuable work "Eliyahu Rabbah" (Sulzbach, 1757), containing discussions on the Oraḥ Ḥayyim, was printed posthumously by his son, whose name is not given. 
2 CONT
2 CONT "Shishah Shiṭṭot," novellæ on six Talmudic treatises, were published by his grandson Elijah b. Wolf Spira 
2 CONT (Fürth, 1768).
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.jewishencyclopedia.com/view.jsp?artid=1017&letter=S
2 CONT
2 CONT https://hebrewbooks.org/41130
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT décédé de la peste en 1713
2 CONT
2 CONT cf GenAmi 45 (septembre 2008)
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT "Die Grabschriften des alten Judenfriedhof in Wien" - Dr. Bernhard Wachstein, Band I pg. 404
