2 NOTE The bride is Lena Herman and the groom Maurice Stein
2 NOTE Bride and groom are my grandparents, Lena Herman and Maurice Stein - Johannesburg, 1909.
2 NOTE Great picture Hanan! Who are they?
3 CONT Love, Gynny
1 OBJE
2 FILE https://media.geni.com/p13/65/ad/75/c7/53444838eda5d66e/rabinowitz_family_original.jpg?hash=d6caf0cc3f76078948c61e723ab7dc6cd34e9a19e8514e75d32471972016565d.1794643199
2 FORM jpg
2 NOTE I was actually interested as a child - hence my taking the picture of my grandparents' wedding to my great aunt Ruby to identify people.  I've noticed with my contemporaries though that they have become much more interested as the
3 CONC y've got older - so there's still hope for your children!
2 NOTE HI Celia, of course, thanks. The pity is that I know many of the names and even knew some of the people in my childhood, I am in contact with some of the descendants but to my kids they might as well have been on the moon!
2 NOTE Hanan - can you see my Geni pics? They are in my album under "Family - photos".  I think the only one with descendants of Elias is the one of my grandparents' wedding.  I'll look to see if I can find any more offline.
2 NOTE Hi Celia please le me see what photos you have!
3 CONT Hanan
2 NOTE Added by Hanan Baradon June 2011: The people in this photograph are Anna, Max, Helena, Elias, Sonya and Paula. Helena is between Max and Elias - theothers are yet to be sorted out but will be soon.
2 NOTE At least some of the same people are in the photo of my grandparents' wedding (Maurice and Lena Stein, who were first cousins. Their mothers were sisters - Sarah and Clara Rabinowitz, who were first cousins of Max, Helena, etc.) T
3 CONC he identifications in that photo were made for me by Ruby Berks, sister of Lena Stein, sometime in the 1960s or early 1970s. Max is there, as are Elias, Sonia and Annie. There is at least one woman unidentified, who could possibly
3 CONC  be Helena or Paula.  She is standing next to Elias.
1 OBJE
2 FILE https://media.geni.com/p5/8166/037/53444836856a5381/Wedding_of_Maurice_and_Lena_Stein_-_JHB_large.jpg?hash=3ffac103390d8f06424cc8fc02c3cdc66517abfd8dad86271a25158dc6605d45.1794643199
2 FORM jpg
2 TITL Wedding of Maurice Stein and Lena Herman
2 NOTE Corrected Date of Wedding from 1909 to 1911
2 NOTE The only other picture I know of is Hanan Baradon's picture of Elias and his children - on this site.  There is one unidentified woman in this picture who I guess may be one of Elias' daughters.
2 NOTE This is a great Pic. Celia are there any other photos of the family at the time of this wedding with Elias's other kids?
2 NOTE This photo is a real gem. Thanks
2 NOTE You're welcome - and thanks for correcting and adding to the Jacobson branch of the Stein family!
2 NOTE Thank you so much for this. I was given a copy of this photograph by my uncle Solly Jacobson ( son of Bertha ) a few years ago.  Now I can fill in many of the unidentified people.
2 NOTE Most of the IDs were made by Ruby Berks (one of the Herman aunts) many years ago.  It's possible some are inaccurate, but I've got them as close as I can.  There is some question as to whether Sam Herman is correctly identified, a
3 CONC s he may not have been in South Africa yet.  If any further research clarifies this, I'll adjust accordingly.
2 NOTE Amazing photo
