1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Rabbi in Wallerstein 1751-63, died 14 Sep 1763 in Wallerstein. Grave 101 in Wallerstein Jewish Cemetery. 
2 CONT
2 CONT For Rapaport - Cohn tree, see http://www.alemannia-judaica.de/images/Images%20246/AC-RAPPAPORT-COHEN.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------
2 CONT From http://www.alemannia-judaica.de/images/HarburgProject/Wallerstein%20Cemetery%20Gravelist%20a.doc
2 CONT
2 CONT RABBI ZWI HIRSCH of Wallerstein (son of Baruch Kahana Rappaport) died 7 Tishrei 524 = 14 Sep 1763 He was Chief Rabbi for the Wallerstein district, succeeded by his two sons [Simcha Bunem Kahana and Isaac Kahana], who adopted the s
2 CONC urname Cohen and later became Chief Rabbis in Bonn – a descendant of these Rabbis founded a book and print shop in Bonn, which still exists today by the name "Bouvier", but it's no longer Jewish since the 1930s.
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife died 11 Jul 1771 in Wallerstein as "Rabbinerin"
2 CONT
2 CONT Per http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=lorenfamily&id=I68923,  Marriage: Spouse Unknown (so check to see if Elke is really his wife's name).  About their son R. Jizchak is written here: http://www.steinheim-
2 CONC institut.de/cgi-bin/epidat?function=Ins&sel=bns&inv=4022 "R. Jizchak stammte aus Wallerstein in Württemberg und war der Sohn von R. Zwi Kahana Rapaport und Elke (beide im Memorbuch von Wallerstein gerühmt, s. Stern S. 43)." Is som
2 CONC eone able to read the memorbuch of Wallerstein?
