1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [http://www.jewishencyclopedia.com/articles/4978-david-samuel-ben-judah-lob '''David Samuel ben Judah Lob'''] 18th century Polish Rabbi and Talmudist. In 1713, he succeeded his father as Av Beit Din of Shidlov when
2 CONC  the latter became rabbi of Cracow. In 1731, he succeeded his father as Av Beit Din of Cracow, holding the position until 1741. He and his brothers signed the controversial cherem against the Ramchal in 1734. R' David Shmuel passe
2 CONC d away in Dzialoszyce in 1751. 
