1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Chief Rabbi of Pintchov (Pinczow, Poland).  Son of Rabbi Yehuda Leib Chief Rabbi of Shidlov, grandson of the Meginei Shlomo. See  [http://hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.aspx?req=3928&st=&pgnum=70&hilite= Ateres Menachem]
2 CONC  and [http://hebrewbooks.org/pdfpager.aspx?req=1203&st=%D7%96%22%D7%A7&pgnum=203&hilite= Sadeh Yehoshua]  He was named "Yosef" after the Meginei Shlomo's father.
2 CONT
2 CONT R. Yosef was nicknamed "Charif," a popular suffix in the family of the Meginei Shlomo, which he earned because of his rabbinic erudition. According to the records of the Vaad Arbaah Artzot, he engaged in a public debate with a Jew
2 CONC ish apostate, Jan Jacob Shidlowski, in 1740 (cited in Sefer Zikaron Pintchov).
2 CONT
2 CONT Descendant of https://www.geni.com/people/Rabbi-of-Tiktin-Yehoshua-Charif-author-Meginei-Shlomo-Pnei-Yehoshua/6000000006709488424, https://www.geni.com/people/R-Meir-Za-k-AB-D-Lwow/6000000008153338399?through=6000000008153033075, 
2 CONC https://www.geni.com/people/Rabbeinu-Yaakov-ben-Asher-Baal-HaTurim/6000000078402787136, https://www.geni.com/people/Rabbeinu-Asher-ben-Yechiel-%D7%A8%D7%90-%D7%A9/6000000078402253666?through=6000000078402787136, and https://www.ge
