1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Rabbi Yitzchak Chajes, author of Zera Yitzchak (1660-1726), disciple of Rabbi Heshel of Cracow, who wrote 13 works, from among which only his composition on the Mishna was published. He was the great grandson of Ra
2 CONC bbi Yitzchak Chajes, Rabbi of Prague, (1538-1610) who wrote "Appei Ravrevei". Two facts are told about his great holiness. One fact concerns his coming before the Holy Throne after his passing. The second is that he said that he w
2 CONC ould see to it, that for the next ten generations, whenever his grandchildren will come to his gravesite to pray in times of troubles, their prayers would be answered.
2 CONT
2 CONT Author
2 CONT * [http://www.hebrewbooks.org/44749 Zera Yitzchak] (on the Mishna)
2 CONT * http://www.hebrewbooks.org/51291 (on Psalms)
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://books.google.com/books?id=MF8LAAAAIAAJ&pg=PR25&lpg=PR25&dq=%D7%90%D7%91%22%D7%93+%D7%97%D7%99%D7%95%D7%AA&source=bl&ots=XTrvxLJWz0&sig=gbMGQt8-f3eR_IwnlwzvFii59NQ&hl=en&sa=X&ei=bKEvU6aOK8Xs0gHDrICQDw&ved=0CCkQ6AEwAA#v=onep
2 CONC age&q=%D7%90%D7%91%22%D7%93%20%D7%97%D7%99%D7%95%D7%AA&f=false Lineage source]
2 CONT
2 CONT Manuscript, commentary on Haftarot by Rabbi Yitzchak Chajes. [Poland, post 1726]. Commentary on Haftarot of Chumash Bereshit. Sermons, combined with composition based on the Kabbalah of the Ari [with title "Megillat Starim" or "M.
2 CONC S.". Heading at head of manuscript: "Commentary on Haftarot written by Rabbi Yitzchak Chajes Av Beit Din of Skolye, 1710". The Kabbalist Ga'on Rabbi Yitzchak Chajes author of Zera Yitzchak (1660-1726, Otzar HaRabbanim 10663), Av B
2 CONC eit Din of Skolye (region of Lvov), among disciples of Rabbi Heschel of Krakow. Authored 13 compositions of which only the composition on the Mishnayot was printed. Grandson of Rabbi Yitzchak Chajes Av Beit Din of Prague (1538-161
2 CONC 0) author of Api Ravreve. Two famous stories demonstrating his holiness became famous; first - of his arrival before the Heavenly court; second - of his statement that any of his descendants for ten generations who would pray at h
2 CONC is grave at time of distress will be granted salvation.
2 CONT
2 CONT ='''MISSING GENERATIONS''' ([https://www.geni.com/projects/Missing-Links-Profiles-with-recorded-famous-Jewish-ancestors-descendants/40488 Missing Links Project])
