2 NSFX The Martyr of Ruzhany
2 _MARNM Za'k
2 NICK The Martyr of Ruzhany
1 NAME Yisrael the Martyr of Ruzhany, ABD Birzai and Zamosc
1 NAME ישראל 'הקדוש מרזינאי' הי"ד" /זקהיים/ הקדוש מרזינאי
2 GIVN ישראל 'הקדוש מרזינאי' הי"ד"
2 SURN זקהיים
2 NSFX הקדוש מרזינאי
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1625
2 PLAC Vienna, Austria
2 ADDR
1 BURI
2 DATE 1659
2 PLAC Ruzhany, Brest, Belarus
2 ADDR
3 CTRY Poland
1 DEAT
2 DATE 9 SEP 1659
1 OCCU Rabbi of Birzai and Zamosc
1 TITL HaKadosh R'
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The Martyrs of Ruzhany (according to the book “Daat Kedoshim”)
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.jewishgen.org/yizkor/ruzhany/ruz010.html
2 CONT ------------
2 CONT
2 CONT This coming Rosh Hashana (2009) marks the 350th anniversary of the death of The Martyrs of Ruzhany.	
2 CONT
2 CONT 	Just before Passover of 1657 in the town of Ruzhany Poland the body of murdered Christian boy was found in the courtyard of a Jewish home.  The Christian community rose up in anger and claimed that the Jews needed the blood for m
2 CONC aking matzos.  The court decreed that if the guilty person did not come forward then the entire Jewish community would be sentenced to death.
2 CONT
2 CONT 	To spare the Jewish community the two Rabbis, R'Israel and R'Tuvia confessed to the murder.  On the second day of Rosh Hashana, Friday the 9th of September 1659 (5420), the death sentence was carried out.
2 CONT
2 CONT 	The sons of R'Israel took the surname Za'k which represents the word 'zera kodesh' meaning 'Holy Seed'.  Later the name was changed to Zackheim which means 'They Are of the Holy Seed'
2 CONT
2 CONT A more complete story can be found here: http://www.jewishgen.org/Yizkor/ruzhany/ruz010.html#Page18
2 CONT
2 CONT ************************************************
2 CONT
2 CONT "...Rabbi Menachem Nachum ben Israel Sak. He was doubtless the son of the martyr Rabbi Israel Sak, a nephew of Rabbi Meir Sak of Lemberg." Cullman, Peter Simonstein. History of the Jewish Community of Schneidemuhl: 1641 to the Hol
2 CONC ocaust. Avotaynu. Bergenfield, NJ 2006.p. 25.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
