1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Braunle can be updated for 1680 birth.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT per Werner Frank:http://www.jewishgen.org/rabbinic/journal/weil_chart2.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT "In the study of Jewish Kippenheim by Jurgen Stude we find the picture of a house entrance at #6 Friedhofstrasse with the Hebrew text "Maharam Weil", reflecting the origin of the two Weil families (Maram and Eliezer), both from St
2 CONC uehlingen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Berthold Rosenthal, in a 1937 note found in his archives at the Leo Baeck Institute, states that the Marum Weil of Kippenheim was called Marx Weyl der Alt in 1748.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Guenther Boll he left Stuehlingen and must have been resident in Kippenheim in the period ; on the other hand Stude says he arrived in Kippenheim in 1740. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter Stein believes him to be Marum, Sandels Sohn.
2 CONT
