2 CONT The rabbis of Kalisz …
2 CONT In 1681, the chief rabbi in Kalisz was Jehudah Rabi, alias Riban (1624-1696). Before he arrived in Kalisz, he had performed the function of the chief rabbi in Tarnów, Olkusz, Sinawa and Tomaszów Mazowiecki. Jehudah was a rector in
2 CONC  the Kalisz yeshiva where he taught the Gemara. The preacher was a practicing cabbalist, that is, he lived an ascetic life. According to the Kabbalah, he wrote personal Pentateuch (Pentateuch scrolls for his own use) introducing s
2 CONC pelling changes as far as the shape of letters was concerned. He based the modifications on a system that he discovered himself. The Pentateuch was housed in the Kalisz Great Synagogue and was read out once a year on a bimah (a pl
2 CONC atform were Torah scrolls are read) during the holiday of Shavuot. When he died, Riban was buried in the old Jewish cemetery in Kalisz.
2 CONT
2 CONT Author: Hila Marcinkowska
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From "Tiferes Aryeh"
2 CONT
2 CONT AB"D Sinever and Kallush
