2 CONT http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~prohel/names/loew/spira/spira_3.html#kolin http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samuel_Loew
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT From the Jewish Encyclopedia (http://jewishencyclopedia.com/articles/10137-low-samuel):
2 CONT
2 CONT LÖW, SAMUEL (called also Samuel Kollin, or Kelin):
2 CONT
2 CONT By: Gotthard Deutsch, S. Mannheimer Talmudist; son of Naṭe ( = Nathan) ha-Levi; born at Kolin, Bohemia, about 1720; died May 20, 1806, at Boskowitz, Moravia, where for nearly sixty years he had presided over a yeshibah. He wrote: 
2 CONC "Maḥaẓit ha-Sheḳel," an extensive subcommentary on Abraham Abele Gombiner's "Magen Abraham" on Shulhan 'Aruk, Oraḥ Ḥayyim (Vienna, 1807-8; 2d ed. 1817; several times reprinted); "Hilkot Niddah" (Lemberg, 1858); and "Hilkot Meliḥah
2 CONC " (ib. 1860). His son Wolf Boskowitz delivered the sermon at his funeral ("Ma'amar Esther," Ofen, 1837). His descendant in the fifth generation, Dr. Max Anton Löw, a convert to Roman Catholicism, was the attorney of the anti-Semit
2 CONC e Deckert ("Mittheilungen der Gesell. zur Abwehr des Antisemitismus," 1896, pp. 45, 48; 1897, pp. 190, 216; "Oest. Wochenschrift," 1896, p. 65).
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samuel_Loew hálévi boskovitzi rabbi, a Machaczith hásekel (Bécs, 1807, Lemberg 1860) szerzője
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Samuel ben Nathan Loew (Kelin) (ca. 1720-1806) (also “Lōw” or “Löw”, Hebrew: שמואל בן נטע הלוי קעלין) was a Talmudist and Halakhist (“Authority on Jewish law”), son of Naṭe ha-Levi (נטע = Nathan), born at Kolin, Bohemia. For nearl
2 CONC y sixty years he presided over a yeshiva at Boskovice, Moravia, where he died on May 20, 1806. He had the title Av Beis Din of Boskowitz.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT His works were published under the name Machatsith haShekel as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT An extensive subcommentary on Abraham Abele Gombiner’s Magen Abraham on Shulhan Aruk, Oraḥ Ḥayyim (Vienna, 1807-1808; 2d ed. 1817; several times reprinted) 
2 CONT
2 CONT A subcommentary on the Shakh on Shulchan Arukh, Yore De’a Hilkhot Niddah (Lemberg, 1858) and Hilkot Meliḥah (ib. 1860) 
2 CONT
2 CONT These commentaries appear nowadays in most editions of the Shulchan Arukh.
2 CONT
2 CONT His son Wolf Boskowitz delivered the sermon at his funeral (Ma’amar Esther, Ofen, 1837). His descendant in the fifth generation, Dr. Max Anton Löw, a convert to Roman Catholicism, was the attorney of the anti-Semite Francis Decker
2 CONC t (Mittheilungen der Gesell. zur Abwehr des Antisemitismus, 1896, pp. 45, 48; 1897, pp. 190, 216; Oest. Wochenschrift, 1896, p. 65).
2 CONT
2 CONT Jewish Encyclopedia bibliography
2 CONT
2 CONT Aaron Walden, Shem ha-Gedolim he-Ḥadash, ii.44, Warsaw, 1880; 
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaac Benjacob, Oẓar ha-Sefarim, p. 321; 
2 CONT
