1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A.B.D. of Ettingen from 1764 on.
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife Leah, daughter of R. Noah Ephraim Fischel, died 1782. Noah Ephraim was the son-in-law of R. Meshullam, A.B.D. Kolomyya, wrote a letter to his son in 1794 while he was in Hamburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT This letter as well as other family documents can be found in Oxford. His sister was the mother of R. Meshullam Igra.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sources=
2 CONT
2 CONT The Unbroken Chain - Neil Rosenstein (1990) Volume 1, Chapter 11, page 96,
2 CONT G 9.8
2 CONT
