2 CONT Kaila and Sulka are two fairly uncommon female names that repeat in the Margolis family in the early 19th century.  I heard from a Margolis family researcher from Russia, who has a very good analytical mind, who hypothesizes that 
2 CONC one of those names is the name of Samuel's wife and the other is the name of Samuel's mother, the first Mordechai's wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel's son, the second Mordechai, named one of his daughters Kaila and one Sulka.
2 CONT
2 CONT The hypothesis is that the first Mordechai’s wife’s name was Kaila and Samuel's wife's name was Sulka. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [Kaila Schick, wife of the first Mordechai Margolis, also might be the same person as the wife of rabbi Yosef Zakheim.  We hypothesize that she remarried after the death of Mordechai Margolis, leaving Vilkaviskis and moving back t
2 CONC o Pruzhany with her younger children Asher and Itel (who later married there and not in the Suwalki area). The extremely high popularity of the name Keila/Kaila among descendants of Mordechai Margolis and Chana Zakheim since 1790s
2 CONC  indicates that she might be the common ancestor of both branches and die old].
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The repetition of the name Kaila in the branches of Samuel (Margolis), his sister Itel (Prozner), and the Pruzhany Zakheim family of Rabbi Yosef Zakheim, are strong evidence that the wife of the first Mordechai Margolis (1) was
2 CONC  named Kaila (Kaila Schick, we know her father was Samuel Schick) and (2) that she married second Yosef Zakheim since the Zakheim family also used this name.  See below.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Kaila in the Margolis family==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT # Kaila Margolis, b. 1815, Daughter of Mordechai Margolis (Samuel, Mordechai); died 1880 in Germany
2 CONT # Kaila Efrati, b. 1830, Great granddaughter of Itel Margolis (Mordechai)
2 CONT # Kaila Margolis, b. 1845, Daughter of Elijah Margolis (Mordechai, Samuel, Mordechai)
2 CONT # Kaila Margolis, b. 1867 Przerosl, Grandaughter of Jacob Bardin (Mordechai, Samuel, Mordechai)
2 CONT # Kaila Ginsberg, b. 1869, Granddaughter of Zvi Hirsh Margolis (Mordechai, Samuel, Mordechai)
2 CONT
2 CONT * “second” Mordechai named his first daughter Kaila (but was Sulka or Kaila his first daughter?)
2 CONT * his son, Jacob, had a granddaughter, Kaila
2 CONT * his son, Elijah, had a daughter, Kaila
2 CONT * his son, Zvi Hirsh, had a granddaughter, Kaila
2 CONT
2 CONT Mordechai’s aunt, Itel Margolis Prozner, had a great granddaughter Kaila b. 1830, so this is Kaila in a different branch than the Samuel branch.  Itel was Samuel's sister.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Kaila in the Zakheim family==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * Keila Gunzberg, daughter of Rabbi Yosef Zakheim, son of Chana Zakheim
2 CONT * Keila Dvora Berlowitz, daughter of Beila Berlowitz, daughter of Chana Zakheim
2 CONT * Hanna Keila Friedland, daughter of Rachel Leah Gunzburg, daughter of Chana Zakheim
2 CONT * Keila Heilprin, daughter of Chaya Heilprin, daughter of Chana Zakheim
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Sulka in the Margolis family==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT # Sulka Margolis b.c. 1808, Kalwaria, Daughter of Mordechai and Hinde (father Ber, mother unknown); died 1860 in Kalwariya
2 CONT # Sulka Bernstein / Tsirelstein b.c. 1850 Merkine, Daughter of Kaila Margolis (Mordechai and Hinde)
2 CONT # Sulka Margolis, b. 1857, Wiesiejai, Daughter of Eliasz/Elijah Margolis (Mordechai + Hinde) and Sora Lewin 
2 CONT # Sulka Liba, b. 1860, Suwalki, daughter of Asher “Isser” Margolis (Elijah, Mordechai + Hinde)
2 CONT # Sula/Sulka “Sophie” Sterling, b. 1863, Granddaughter of Sulka Margolis (see above #1), also wife of Mordechai “Marcus” Margolis, her cousin.  Daughter of Abraham Sterling and Miriam “Majorie”
2 CONT # Sulka Sterling b.1883 in Bakalerzewo, Grandaughter of Sulka Margolis (#1 above)   Daughter of Nota Sterling and Chaya Feyga Borowska
2 CONT
2 CONT Update June 2017: According to Neil Rosenstein, Vol I, Third Edition of The Unbroken Chain, page 42, fn 93, the wife of R. Mordechai Schick was born in Tykocin and settled in Vilkaviskis. This is taken from the HaMaggid obituary o
2 CONC f Elijah Margolis, a descendant and Lithuanian rabbi and father of a dynasty of rabbis.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT * The Unbroken Chain by Dr. Neil Rosenstein, Vol 1 2nd edition, page 18. Paragraph G9.4
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-1-36803721-3-11072/wife-of-mordechai-margolies-born-schick-in-myheritage-family-trees?indId=externalindividual-7baab7c35d7bd3a1ab628a05c4d21cd3&mrid=955db389c4652a0d8bcea6ce
2 CONC 545ec885 MyHeritage Family Trees] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jun 18 2017, 4:17:34 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT She might be the same person as the wife of Mordechai Margolis of Vilkaviskis and could move back to Pruzhany after his death  with her younger children Asher and Itel (who later married there), and remarry rabbi Yosef. The extrem
2 CONC ely high popularity of the name Keila/Kaila among descendants of Mordechai Margolis and Chana Zakheim since 1790s indicates that she might be the common ancestor of both branches and die old. Unfortunately, there are no revision l
2 CONC ists from Pruzhany availible online.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kaila in the Zakheim family:
2 CONT * Keila Gunzberg, daughter of Rabbi Yosef Zakheim, son of Chana Zakheim
2 CONT * Keila Dvora Berlowitz, daughter of Beila Berlowitz, daughter of Chana Zakheim
2 CONT * Hanna Keila Friedland, daughter of Rachel Leah Gunzburg, daughter of Chana Zakheim
2 CONT * Keila Heilprin, daughter of Chaya Heilprin, daughter of Chana Zakheim
2 CONT
2 CONT Kaila in the Margolis family
2 CONT
2 CONT # Kaila Margolis, b. 1815, Daughter of Mordechai Margolis (Samuel, Mordechai); died 1880 in Germany
2 CONT # Kaila Efrati, b. 1830, Great granddaughter of Itel Margolis (Mordechai)
2 CONT # Kaila Margolis, b. 1845, Daughter of Elijah Margolis (Mordechai, Samuel, Mordechai)
2 CONT # Kaila Margolis, b. 1867 Przerosl, Grandaughter of Jacob Bardin (Mordechai, Samuel, Mordechai)
2 CONT # Kaila Ginsberg, b. 1869, Granddaughter of Zvi Hirsh Margolis (Mordechai, Samuel, Mordechai)
2 CONT
2 CONT * “second” Mordechai named his first daughter Kaila (but was Sulka or Kaila his first daughter?)
2 CONT * his son, Jacob, had a granddaughter, Kaila
2 CONT * his son, Elijah, had a daughter, Kaila
2 CONT * his son, Zvi Hirsh, had a granddaughter, Kaila
2 CONT
2 CONT Mordechai’s aunt, Itel Margolis Prozner, had a great granddaughter Kaila b. 1830, so this is Kaila in a different branch than the Samuel branch.  Itel was Samuel's sister.
