1 NOTE {geni:about_me} G11.1 R. (Moses) Mordecai Katzenellenbogen, signed his name in Luchot HaEidut, Altona, 1775, with the other rabbis of Lublin.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source
2 CONT
2 CONT The Unbroken Chain - Neil Rosenstein (3rd edition) Volume 3, Chapter 8, page 422.
2 CONT
2 CONT Please note that according to the above source, some authors have confused him with his uncle of the same name, concluding incorrectly that the nephew was the one who served as Rabbi of Kedainiai between 1782-95. However, the cens
2 CONC us records make clear that it was Mordecai, son of Meshullam Zelman, and not Mordecai, son of Menachem Nachum who served as a rabbi during this period.
2 CONT
2 CONT It should be noted that in some instances, he has also been confused with his 2nd cousin, who was also a Rabbi Moses, and also a son of a Rabbi Menachem Nachum!  These two 2nd cousins were great-grandsons of R' David Katzenellenpo
2 CONC gen, ABD Kedainiai.  
2 CONT
2 CONT According to [https://keidaner.com/181rabbis-of-keidan/] he died in Keidaniai in 1810.
2 CONT
2 CONT If you follow this link, you will see that a comment has been added by me, regarding the confusion between the two 2nd cousins.
