1 CONT G5.1. Jacob Shor, A.B.D. Lutzk, Brest and Brody. He was the author of Beit Yaakov published Venice 1693. He is mentioned in the following works: 1. Beit Hillel by Hillel, son of Naftali Hirsch, published, Dyhernfurth 1691. 2. Beit
1 CONC  Yaakov by Jacob Zausmer, published, Dyhernfurth 1696. 3. Responsa Geonim Batrai. 4. Chelkat Mechokek. Jacob was a pupil of R. Abraham, son of Benjamin Aaron (of Slonik, author of Masa'ot Binyamin), A.B.D. Brest. His signature app
1 CONC ears in years 1647  and 1649 in the Pinkas (Minutes) of Lithuania following that of Jonah Teomim, A.B.D. of Grodno. His signatures while as Brest appeared in 1650, 1651,  and 1655. He also was the author of unpublished responsa an
1 CONC d was married to Hannah, daughter of Isaiah, son of Moses Lazers of Vilna.
