1 CONT G5.4. Israel of Neshov, married the daughter of R. Samuel Kalisher, was  from the second marriage. He died "tender in days" according to his epitaph in the old Lublin cemetery. He died  on Sunday, 6th of Nisan, 1639.  He had lived
1 CONC  in Lublin where his paternal grandfather had established a synagogue called  by his name, Saul Wahl, but also known as the furriers' synagoguw (or the "runners" shul - "der loifer-shul"). Descendants of the family in Lublin remai
1 CONC ned as custodians of this synagogue for many generations.
